# WP-273: the site's file c.o is edited and the site stays at 0xff8: the
# stored patch (keyed by the old c.o) becomes a Fill hole, and the new
# site's patch is appended after it; each hop adds a hole and a patch
# inside the island's capacity.
proves: an update that edits an erratum 843419 site's file writes the old patch as a zero Fill hole and appends the new site's patch (P-I1: the island's bytes are the map's); every hop is an update, equivalent to the full link
source: spec/landed/incr/WP-271.md §4 (e843419_changed_file_patch_hole), WP-273
edit A: c.S
hops: -, A, -, A
link: a.o c.o
compilers: gcc
targets: a64
not kiln: assembly (.S): kiln compiles C++ only; the shape is written in the assembly
not x64: erratum 843419 is AArch64's (`--fix-cortex-a53-843419` is refused on x86-64, cli rows); x86-64 has no islands, its updates call no re-plan
nolibc: yes
options: --fix-cortex-a53-843419
